{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>You have wearied</b> — We know from another passage that the honored HaShem cannot be wearied, and how can His deeds weary Him? Rather, it is in human language, that He will no longer tolerate evildoers — were it not good in His eyes, He would not let them act. And if you say, He will yet execute judgment — when was this, and where is He? Why does He not execute judgment?! And this prophecy is for the future; and first Elijah will come, as is written at the end of the book."], :book :malachi, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {0 "The phrase 'from another passage' (פרשה אחרת) likely refers to Isaiah 40:28; left as 'another passage' without resolving, following Ibn Ezra's generic reference."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Malachi -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/malachi"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:13:26.560471497Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}